{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/816447-spirits-as-a-playable-option","id":816447,"title":"Spirits as a playable option.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-25T15:06:23-08:00","id":816447,"title":"Spirits as a playable option.","content":"Am I the only person whos wanted a little box for playing as a spirit, thinking doing so would add a degree of perspective on the umbra...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T18:01:20-08:00","id":816548,"title":"","content":"It would certainly be interesting, though it seems like most of the spirits that are important in W:tA are pretty alien in their mindset and would be very difficult (and perhaps not even that fun) to play correctly. There is the possibility of playing somebody possessed by a spirit where the nature of the human moderates that of the spirit so as to be approachable for a player. I think that it might take a bit of fleshing out to make standard spirits playable, I would be curious to see attempts though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T00:01:37-08:00","id":816713,"title":"","content":"Having a player act as the the pack's totem might be a lot of fun. Characterization would not be a huge problem- it would be weird and different as a roleplaying experience, but not insurmountable. I would be more interested in making interesting stats for the totem character, since spirit statistics are pretty boring (not a lot of nuance between three traits and a handful of charms). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T03:53:53-08:00","id":816767,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> : I agree. In fact, the authors seem to do so too. There are actually rules for exactly what you are proposing: The Kami-rules out of &quot;Posessed&quot;.<br /> Just make sure, to scale them appropriatly in comparison to the shapechangers in the group. Kami tend to start way lower than garou and should get some extra love before being introduced into the campain in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Concerning actual spirits as characters:<br /> If you would want to do it (it seems interesting enough), I recoment to check out &quot;Mage the Ascention, Ascentions right hand&quot;. Its an old book (and yes, I know its mage, not werewolf) detailing familiars of different kinds. I`d say as a house rule: build the &quot;body&quot; of the spirit using the rules found in ascentions right hand, and the supernatural powers as detailed in werewolf the apocalyse.<br /> Makes the whole play a lot smoother than using the will/gnosis/rage pools to do literally anything the spirit atempts to do, and allows for a more comparible character sheet to the normal were-wolf ones.<br /> &quot;Materialisation&quot; should be a must, so that the player can actually contribute to a session, wich is mostly human-world. He should make sure however, to stay out of sight or do something else to prevent raising to much attention (a spirit of an existig animal might have less problems with that, than truely alien looking spirits).<br /> I`d add the same limitations on &quot;modern&quot; skills that a lupus character has (exept for a technology-spirit of course) and you should be ready to go.<br /> Here too, keep an eye on the power-distribution, so everyone is more or less on the same level of might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6112,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","user":"Seki","date":". 01-26-2016, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T08:31:33-08:00","id":816906,"title":"","content":"With players tending to aim for special snowflakes and means to not reflect the archtype of tribe or auspice it seems odd to aim to play a being that is basically the personification of being typecast. I mean, spirits have types and their midset is kind of limited - only the stronger one have something that resembles free will. So they don't make good characters in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Sure, if you go strict by the core book, animal spirits are ghosts of dead animals, so you can play the ghost of another players puppy. But is a dog a suitable character, I don't thinks so - lupus born at least have human level intelligence.<br /> An ancestor spirit might work, but they to, are bound to act according to what ever they represent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T17:35:44-08:00","id":817265,"title":"","content":"Bygone Bestiary has great rules for this. Just create the beast as per those rules, and allow them to buy Charms, Gifts and/or Redes for their powers. Gnosis and Rage you can improvise. Start off with seven dots between the two or five each, or whatever you think is appropriate. Then the character will be roughly equivalent to a player character of the normal splats.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You could base Rage off the highest Physical Attribute and Gnosis off the highest Social or Mental Attribute (before the Freebies stage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 01-30-2016, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T17:38:57-08:00","id":817269,"title":"","content":"It's all fun and games till another player binds your character into a fetish....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T02:15:02-08:00","id":818299,"title":"","content":"Depending on the rules used, fetish binding has to be voluntarily. But binding to a place or object with the rite of bindung, which is less permanent, doesn't require cooperation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T03:03:17-08:00","id":818313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/816447-spirits-as-a-playable-option?p=817269#post817269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's all fun and games till another player binds your character into a fetish....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Player who'd do that isn't much different than one who would kill/injure other physical pcs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T03:53:54-08:00","id":818322,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure Spirits are supposed to be playable characters. First of all, most of them cannot interact with the real world in a proper way. Second of all, Spirits are downright alien. And it's not alien in a - oh i'm human with strange values or exotic culture...<br /> <br /> It's alien in a literally non-human thought process kind of way. Spirits exists as echoes of events, emotions, fears, creatures and ideas in our world. They live for the stimulus that made them and their whole existence is in serving and propagating these same stimuli to increase their own power and further increase their own purvey.<br /> <br /> There is a reason why you actually need a power to even understand what they are trying to say, as they commune through only the impulses and concepts they understand. This is their normal thought process... this isn't a language in any kind of way we understand, it's literally expression within the purvey of what they represent.<br /> <br /> The only spirits who actually have agendas that might be relatable to us are stuck and defined by the realms they inhabit, making them poor choices for player characters.<br /> <br /> As such, playing spirits in a Werewolf game does not really suit the style and theme of spirits as the mysterious beings that the Werewolves are forced to deal with. Playing a game about spirits would be more like playing Nobilis then like playing Werewolf the Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:06:19-08:00","id":818482,"title":"","content":"If I, as a storyteller, can play the weird umbral beings, I think a skilled player could too. Obviously gafflings are off the table, they are too unintelligent to be compelling. Again, even with an alien mindset, a pack totem has a stake in the story at hand. A totem won't just be concerned about 'hummingbird things' or 'coyote things,' they have a strong interest in seeing their pack succeed. Spirits are characters too, just really strange ones with unusual strengths and limitations. I don't get why there is this 'oh spirits are too weird, they are just beyond play-ability.'<br /> <br /> Bullcrap.<br /> <br /> Lovecraftian horrors aren't real. I have been roleplaying a long time, and this is a story game, told by <i>people</i>. We tell stories about people, because that is what we are, and to some degree, all we can conceive of, at a fundamental level. What we can do is portray facsimiles of the alien, of the other, but usually what we end up with are quirky and strange <i>people.</i> We can reduce spirits to something less than human, make them animals or forces, or some mix thereof, but these are certainly not of a completely alien mindset, much less an ineffable one.<br /> <br /> We can't <i>really be alien beings, </i>we are all just playing pretend and doing our best to give voice to what should be, in the context of the story, a weird inhuman thing.<br /> <br /> If a player can do well making their in-game voice be a strange alien facsimile, I will let him play a spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:39:27-08:00","id":818509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/816447-spirits-as-a-playable-option?p=818482#post818482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can't <i>really be alien beings, </i>we are all just playing pretend and doing our best to give voice to what should be, in the context of the story, a weird inhuman thing.<br /> <br /> If a player can do well making their in-game voice be a strange alien facsimile, I will let him play a spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey. I love Nobilis. It's not that I don't believe we couldn't portray a spirit, it's more that actually playing spirits completley changes the tone of the campaign. It's a major impact on the plot and really sets the tone. Even if it doesn't, you change the party dynamic drastically with a character that has none of the physical concerns and motivations the rest of the cast does and that cannot meaningfuly interact with the strictly physical world. It's very similar to why I would dissaprove AI characters in Shadowrun as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:46:42-08:00","id":818516,"title":"","content":"Well, to offer an example from another game series, Cole from Dragon Age is a great example of a spirit made playable.<br /> <br /> Video showing his motivation/powers; <a href=\"https://youtu.be/cMV7XLpxTWU\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/cMV7XLpxTWU</a><br /> <br /> I think a spirit character -can- work, if the spirit is given motivation to care for the physical (purpose to fulfil there) and a reason to stay manifested (Geas? Ban? A promise)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:52:06-08:00","id":818526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/816447-spirits-as-a-playable-option?p=818509#post818509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey. I love Nobilis. It's not that I don't believe we couldn't portray a spirit, it's more that actually playing spirits completley changes the tone of the campaign. It's a major impact on the plot and really sets the tone. Even if it doesn't, you change the party dynamic drastically with a character that has none of the physical concerns and motivations the rest of the cast does and that cannot meaningfuly interact with the strictly physical world. It's very similar to why I would dissaprove AI characters in Shadowrun as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but again, if we are talking about a pack totem, this spirit is already going to be along for the ride as it is. Motivation should not be a big concern, since the pack totem will largely want what the pack wants. Give it the ability to materialize when it absolutely has to, and maybe some other nice support charms, and it could work pretty well, methinks, but I do agree, it will be a tonal shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T02:57:08-08:00","id":819075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/816447-spirits-as-a-playable-option?p=818313#post818313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player who'd do that isn't much different than one who would kill/injure other physical pcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>OffPlay, maybe. But InPlay it is okay to bind spirits and especially waning theurges aren't very polite about it. So, you are forcing the players into a position, where they treat spirit differently because it is a PC not an NPC.<br /> <br /> I guess, that is the case with garou NPCs and garou PCs, too, but still I find it undesirable.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Pack Totem<br /> I don't think the pack totem is along for the ride, all the time. I mean, the pack totem avatar wouldn't follow the pack into the city in the penumbra, for it would enter the territories of other spirits and probably get into a lot of danger if trying to follow the pack (and if the pack separates, whom would it follow?). Also, the pack totem avatars aren't that strong.<br /> <br /> Actually, a rival pack or BSD might if they have a competent theurge try to summon the pack totem avatar and kill it, just to cut the pack off from their totem. Sure, a new avatar would eventually appear, but this would take time and during that time, I would not grant totem boni.<br /> <br /> &quot;the totem is often with the pack&quot; was a feature one had to buy, iirc. But, like I said, it doesn't make that much sense, unless the avatar materializes to accompany the pack.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}